  "notes": [
    "frame-09 (sunset, sun on horizon, PM) not generated: reuse frame-05 for PM altitude 0 until supplied.",
    "Sources 1672x941 (frame-08: 1536x864) resampled to 1920x1080 with Lanczos + light unsharp mask.",
    "align: [scale, x, y] in 1920x1080 px (transform-origin 0 0) lines a frame up with its neighbours. Frames 06 and 07 came out about 10% wider; 07 is fitted to 06 (they crossfade at golden hour into mid-morning) and checked by eye against 06 and 08. The frames are redrawn, not just relit, so no alignment is exact: sky.js shows one frame at a time and dissolves between them.",
    "transitions: for each handover A->B, mid-a = half-way light (blurred A and B mixed) + A's fine detail, mid-b = the same light + B's detail (made by tv-home/tools/landscape-transitions.html). The home plays A -> mid-a -> mid-b -> B: the light moves with one frame's detail at a time, and only the short mid-a -> mid-b step mixes two drawings."
